  "title": "tshark: Do not cleanup or init a null edt when resetting memory",
  "description": "Trying to call epan_dissect_cleanup or epan_dissect_init on a\nnull edt will fail an assertion (or crash.) This only applies to\nreading a capture file (including from a pipe) where we don't need\nto dissect (because we're just writing to a new file format without\nfiltering, for example.)\n\nWe perhaps don't really need to reset the epan memory at all either,\nsince we shouldn't have allocated much if we're not dissecting.",
