      "id": "26bd59a9bdd6703842d036d2c77546a30b1001c6",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2387322737,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Seems like this could be achieved by making the call to `reset_epan_mem()` in `process_cap_file_single_pass()` depend on `if (edt)` or `if (do_dissection)`.\n\nOne other thing that struck me as odd is the difference of the `visible` parameter for `epan_dissect_new()` and `reset_epan_mem()`. The first takes `output_fields_num_fields(output_fields) == 0` into consideration, while the latter does not. This for every use of `reset_epan_mem()`.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2398962,
            "username": "JaapKeuter",
